#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8a6a4f-38ce-5ece-bdcb-6f2b58e2605c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "121c55cc-404a-53e7-81f7-6edba34b0796" :question/math-academy-id "e-12956" :question/problem "What is the solution to $7z \\lt -21$?" :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $7$. To isolate $z$, we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $7$. Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7z & < - 21 \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & < \\frac{-21}{7} \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & < - 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $7$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{7z}{7} & < - 3 \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & < - 3 \\\\ z & < - 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z \\lt -3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054400 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281841fb-287e-597a-abb1-3917212e0dcb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "7424a287-2269-5044-abb7-1004b3826aca" :question/math-academy-id "e-12957" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-6x \\leq -7$." :question/worked-solution "The variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $-6$. To isolate $x$, we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-6$. Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6x & \\le - 7 \\\\ \\frac{-6x}{-6} & \\ge\\frac{-7}{-6} \\\\ \\frac{-6x}{-6} & \\ge\\frac{7}{6}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-6$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-6x}{-6} & \\ge \\frac{7}{6} \\\\ \\frac{-6x}{-6} & \\ge \\frac{7}{6} \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{7}{6}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\geq \\dfrac{7}{6}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "200fc394-b299-5114-8f39-e6265f3c1166" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a One-Step Inequality With Fractions When Flipping Is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "82a9a75f-ab0e-54c3-9a0d-82c8497714cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12958" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-\\dfrac{y}{8} \\leq -4$." :question/worked-solution "The variable $y$ is being *divided* by $8$. To isolate $y$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-8$.\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{y}{8} & \\le - 4 \\\\ (-8) \\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8}) & \\ge(-8) \\cdot (-4) \\\\ (-8) \\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8}) & \\ge32\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(-8) \\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8}) & \\ge 32 \\\\ (-8) \\cdot (-\\frac{y}{8}) & \\ge 32 \\\\ 8 \\cdot \\frac{y}{8} & \\ge 32\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $8$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\cdot \\frac{y}{8} & \\ge 32 \\\\ \\frac{8y}{8} & \\ge 32 \\\\ \\frac{8y}{8} & \\ge 32 \\\\ y & \\ge 32\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\ny \\geq 32\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b0cad0-354b-5c4c-9fe2-3aceff7e5b6e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/id #uuid "1154ded3-0841-5358-980c-15c0f1841e82" :question/math-academy-id "e-12959" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-9 \\leq -3z$." :question/worked-solution "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $-3$. To isolate $z$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-3$. Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & \\le - 3z \\\\ \\frac{-9}{-3} & \\ge\\frac{-3z}{-3} \\\\ 3 & \\ge\\frac{-3z}{-3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-3$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & \\ge \\frac{-3z}{-3} \\\\ 3 & \\ge \\frac{-3z}{-3} \\\\ 3 & \\ge z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember that we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\nz \\leq 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nz \\leq 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b0cad0-354b-5c4c-9fe2-3aceff7e5b6e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89ee6cbb-2000-5184-8496-de0a77ba263f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051669} {:answer/id #uuid "adba1f7c-f78f-51f7-ae93-6df08b4263b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051670} {:answer/id #uuid "081511da-a9ed-57e8-ab16-3a644c71d383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le - 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051671} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc72615-e65b-51cf-ab14-ef2e1ffbe8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051672} {:answer/id #uuid "2e54ec53-ac88-567f-b5aa-3bd0aa951d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051673